    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0154" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg80"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 23, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my notes of the 7th and 17th
                    instant, I have the honor to enclose for the further information of the proper
                    authorities of her Majesty’s government a copy of a despatch of the 13th
                    instant, from M. M. Jackson, esq., the United States consul at Halifax,
                    respecting the proposed hostile expeditions against the United States from
                    Canada.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d135-a1.xml" xpointer="d135-a1"/>
